<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" style="margin-bottom:3rem;">
      <span class="section-label">Quality Assurance</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">Streetwear Quality Control</h2>
    </div>

    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
      Quality control for streetwear begins with fabric inspection before cutting. We verify fabric weight, hand-feel, color consistency, and shrinkage rates. Heavyweight fabrics require special attention to ensure consistent weight and texture across the roll. Any fabric that doesn't meet specifications is rejected and replaced. Our fabric suppliers are OEKO-TEX certified, providing traceability and assurance that materials meet international standards for quality and safety. This pre-production inspection prevents quality issues downstream and ensures your streetwear starts with premium materials.
    </p>

    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1.5rem;">
      During production, we implement inline quality checks at multiple stages specific to streetwear construction. Cutting supervisors verify pattern accuracy and ensure proper grain direction for consistent fit. Sewing line leaders monitor stitching quality, seam consistency, and construction standards including drop-shoulder alignment, cuff attachment, and pocket construction. Our production floor follows ISO 9001 quality management procedures with documented quality checkpoints. Any garment that doesn't meet quality standards during inline inspection is flagged for rework or rejection.
    </p>

    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1.5rem;">
      Final inspection occurs after printing, embroidery, and finishing are complete. Our quality control team conducts AQL (Acceptable Quality Limit) inspections checking print alignment, embroidery quality, stitching defects, sizing accuracy, and overall finish. We measure a statistically significant sample from each production batch to ensure overall quality meets or exceeds your specifications. Defective garments are separated, documented, and either reworked or replaced. We maintain acceptable defect rates below 2.5%, which is below industry standards.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

